+++ b/docs/connect-hermes.md
@@ -54,3 +54,10 @@ an approved client advertising `caps.pet.asset_channel: 4`. The current profile'
 active pet is converted to PNG with alpha. Pillow is optional; unavailable or invalid
 pet art leaves conversations working. See the [pet wire contract](protocol.md#optional-pet-assets-wear-extension).
 This is an opt-in extension; no personal art is bundled with the plugin.
+
+Optional phone BYOK speech: set `platforms.gadget.extra.enable_client_tts: true`.
+The watch must offer client speech and receive its acknowledgement. These sessions
+keep readable replies and receive one final speech event, with an optional configured
+profile voice ID. Automatic server TTS is suppressed for them; /voice off still wins.
+The phone's own key stays on the phone. Default/stock/no-phone sessions use server TTS.
+See the [wire contract](protocol.md#optional-client-side-speech-wear-extension).
diff --git a/docs/protocol.md b/docs/protocol.md
index 47c1390..b05124a 100644
--- a/docs/protocol.md
+++ b/docs/protocol.md
@@ -259,3 +259,29 @@ Limit two assets, 2 MiB compressed each, 3.2 million pixels per asset, grid dime
 The reference server paces chunks at 20 ms and caps the entire delivery at 30 seconds.
 Metadata paths and symlinks must stay within the profile pet directory. RGB565 image
 channel 2 is unchanged. PNG preserves alpha; no new native Python dependency is needed.
+
+### Optional client-side speech (Wear extension)
+
+Disabled by default (`platforms.gadget.extra.enable_client_tts: true` opts in).
+A device offers `caps.tts:"client"` only while its configured phone speech service
+is reachable/ready. A supporting hub replies `welcome.tts:"client"`, optionally
+with `voice` (profile ElevenLabs voice ID, never an API key). An absent acknowledgement
+means stock server speech. Direct/no-phone reconnections must omit this capability.
+
+An approved acknowledged session receives normal readable reply/delta frames plus
+`tts.speak {id,text,turn?,voice?}` for final, non-interim replies. Text is capped at
+4096 characters. IDs suppress duplicate identical final replies within a turn,
+with a 64-event in-memory bound; a distinct turn can repeat the same words. Outside
+turns, each final message is a separate event. Never synthesize transcripts/deltas,
+replay interrupted inputs, or replay a cancelled speech event on reconnect. Late
+turn-tagged speech must be ignored after cancellation or turn replacement. The
+adapter respects speak_replies and chat /voice off, suppresses automatic server TTS
+for client sessions, and disables its server streaming TTS seam for them.
+
+The phone speech channel is separate from the Hermes connection: opting in discloses
+final reply text to the phone and the user's provider, while device enrollment/HMAC
+remain protected inside watch-owned TLS. Keys stay in the phone vault and never enter
+Hermes messages. Provider/API failure leaves text readable and prompts correction or
+server mode on reconnect; do not silently make a second paid synthesis request.
+Stock devices/servers need no change, and existing explicit voice attachments are not
+reclassified as automatic client speech.
